{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-183430",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "Let's recall the following grammatical constructions for the implication $P⇒Q:$\n\n- If $P,$ then $Q$\n\n- $P$ only if $Q$\n\n- $Q$ if $P$\n\n- $P$ implies $Q$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine the given options.\n\n- Option I reads\n\n$$\n\\text{if}\\,{{x\\in Z}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)},\\,\\text{then}\\,{{x\\in N}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $Q(x)⇒P(x).$ $\\,\\times $\n\n- Option II reads\n\n$$\n{{x\\in Z}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\\,\\text{if}\\,{{x\\in N}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Option III reads\n\n$$\n{{x\\in N}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{implies}\\,{{x\\in Z}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\n- Option IV reads\n\n$$\n{{x\\in N}_{⏟}}_{P(x)}\\,\\text{only if}\\,{{x\\in Z}_{⏟}}_{Q(x)}\n$$\n\nwhich corresponds to $P(x)⇒Q(x).$ $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II, III and IV only.\"",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
